\newlabel{fig:superimposed-axis}{{8a}{10}{BNS non-spinning ($1.4 - 1.4\,M_\odot $) superimposed signals. The TT-SNR MAP clearly encodes the presence of two signals that are closely separated in time and nearly identical in parameter space. An interference-like pattern emerges from the superposition of the signal representations produced by the template-based SNR time series, highlighting the TT-SNR MAP’s ability to capture overlapping events.\relax }{figure.caption.19}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:superimposed-axis}{{a}{10}{BNS non-spinning ($1.4 - 1.4\,M_\odot $) superimposed signals. The TT-SNR MAP clearly encodes the presence of two signals that are closely separated in time and nearly identical in parameter space. An interference-like pattern emerges from the superposition of the signal representations produced by the template-based SNR time series, highlighting the TT-SNR MAP’s ability to capture overlapping events.\relax }{figure.caption.19}{}}
